            <ArticleTitle>Left-circumflex coronary artery to right atrium fistula with saccular aneurysm and its endovascular treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>114-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The combination of coronary artery aneurysm and coronary artery fistula is infrequent. A saccular aneurysm of a branch of the left-circumflex coronary artery associated with multiple fistulae to the right atrium was observed on a coronary angiogram performed in a 47-year-old female. Multidetector computed tomography coronary angiography detailed the anatomy of the abnormal coronary artery. An embolization with a microcoil was performed and the aneurysm sac was excluded.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
